-- title:
--   Branches of A ⊗_{Z_0} C at a root of Φ_q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $Z_0$ a commutative ring, $C$ a commutative $Z_0$-algebra and $w \in C$ an element with $\Phi_q(w) = 0$, where $\Phi_q$ is the $q$-th cyclotomic polynomial over $Z_0$ and the evaluation is via the structure map of $C$; let $A$ be a commutative $Z_0$-algebra which is a domain and $\zeta \in A$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Write $T = A \otimes_{Z_0} C$ and, for $\mu \in A$, call $\mu \otimes 1 - 1 \otimes w \in T$ the branch element at $\mu$. Four assertions are made. First, the product of the branch elements over $\mu$ ranging in the finite set `primitiveRoots q A` of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $A$ vanishes in $T$. Secondly, every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $T$ contains the branch element at some primitive $q$-th root of unity $\mu$. Thirdly, for an arbitrary ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $T$ and arbitrary $\mu, \mu' \in A$, if $\mathfrak p$ contains the branch elements at $\mu$ and at $\mu'$ then $(\mu - \mu') \otimes 1 \in \mathfrak p$. Fourthly, for $\mathfrak p$ a minimal prime of $T$ and arbitrary $\mu \in A$ such that $\mathfrak p$ contains the branch element at $\mu$, the image of $\mathfrak p$ in the branch quotient $T/J_\mu$, where $J_\mu$ is the principal ideal generated by that branch element, is a minimal prime of $T/J_\mu$, and there is a ring isomorphism $T/\mathfrak p \cong (T/J_\mu)/\overline{\mathfrak p}$.
--
--   This is the branch decomposition of a tensor product $A \otimes_{Z_0} C$ in which $C$ carries a root of $\Phi_q$ and $A$ contains all primitive $q$-th roots of unity: the spectrum is covered by the closed subschemes cut out by the branch elements, and each minimal prime is accounted for on one branch. It is used in the analysis of full-level modular curves, where the statements about completions at primes of the relevant moduli rings and their unramifiedness are reduced to the corresponding statements on a single branch.
